1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,695
What if a day lasted forty eight
hours? Imagine Earth gradually
spinning more slowly, not stopping
suddenly.

2
00:00:06,695 --> 00:00:12,550
Our trip around the Sun stays the
same. The change in this thought
experiment is the daily rotation.

3
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:19,090
A place could spend longer under
sunlight, then longer in darkness,
reshaping daily heating and cooling.

4
00:00:19,090 --> 00:00:25,290
Rotation also matters for weather.
Predicting the new winds would
require a model, not just a guess.

5
00:00:25,290 --> 00:00:31,835
Living things follow biological
rhythms. A longer light and dark
cycle would challenge those familiar
schedules.

6
00:00:31,835 --> 00:00:37,660
A longer day would not simply double
everything. The interesting question
is how the whole system adapts.
